[<<cite:FGR2>>] Let $v \in T_n(\mathbb C)$ be generic. Then the $\mathfrak{gl}(n)$-module structure on $V(T(v))$ is defined by the formulas:

\begin{equation}
E_{m\ell} (T(v+z))= \sum_{\sigma \in \Phi_{m\ell}} e_{m\ell} (\sigma (v+z)) T(v+z+\sigma(\varepsilon_{m\ell})),
\end{equation}

for $z \in T_{n-1}({\mathbb Z})$ and $1 \leq m ,\ \ell \leq n$. Moreover, $V(T(v))$ is a Gelfand-Tsetlin module with action of $\Ga$ given by the formulas in Theorem <<ref:action of Gamma on fd modules>>.
